.TH CUMCAMS-DL 1 "2026-11-13" "cumcams-dl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cumcams-dl \- download a cumcams.cc video over HLS, split across CDN edge nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cumcams-dl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIURL\fR
.P
.B cumcams-dl
\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR
\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR
\fIhttps://cumcams.cc/video/\fR\fIID\fR\fB/play\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cumcams-dl
downloads an archived show from
.BR cumcams.cc ,
which exposes only an HLS
.I index.m3u8
playlist rather than a progressive file.
A two hour recording is roughly 3900 two-second segments, so a serial
downloader spends most of its time on connection setup and ends up far below
the available bandwidth.
.P
The tool walks the same anonymous chain the web player uses: the video page
supplies a
.I mid
cookie plus
.IR data-video-id " and " data-token ,
.B GET /api/video/\fIID\fB?token=\fI...
returns the player HTML, and that HTML contains a signed
.I index.m3u8
URL.
No account, cookie file, or clearance token is required.
.P
The segment list is then split into chunks, fetched with
.BR yt-dlp (1)
and
.BR \-N ,
and the finished chunks are concatenated and remuxed to Matroska by
.BR ffmpeg (1)
without re-encoding.
Sustained throughput is capped at about 2 MB/s per client IP, so a two hour
recording takes somewhere near an hour no matter which client is used.
.P
Chunks are kept in a work directory keyed by video id, so an interrupted run
resumes at the first missing chunk rather than starting over.
The signed stream URL expires after roughly eighty minutes; because the
script resolves a fresh one on every invocation, a re-run simply works.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory for the finished file. Default:
.IR ~/Videos/cumcams .
.TP
.BI \-n " NAME"
Output basename, without extension. Default: derived from the stream path,
e.g.\&
.IR nana_stolass_2026-09-29_13-16 .
.TP
.BI \-j " N"
Concurrent fragments, passed to
.BR yt\-dlp " \-N" .
Default:
.BR 2 .
Sustained throughput is capped per client IP at about 2 MB/s regardless of
this value: runs with
.BR \-N " 1, 2 and 4"
all measured 2.05 MB/s.
Raising it therefore buys nothing and only increases the chance of tripping
the connection shield described under
.BR BEHAVIOUR .
.TP
.BI \-\-nodes " N"
Number of edge nodes to spread across. Default:
.BR 1 ,
which is correct for this CDN.
Raising it only helps during the short burst allowance that follows an idle
period, and costs nothing to try when a download is already running cold.
.TP
.BI \-\-chunk\-size " N"
Segments per chunk. Default:
.BR 100 ,
about three and a half minutes of video. Keep this small: the connection
shield described under
.B BEHAVIOUR
can cut a transfer at any moment, and this is the amount of work a single cut
can throw away. Smaller chunks cost more
.BR yt\-dlp
invocations but lose less.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-segments " N"
Download only the first
.I N
segments. Default
.B 0
means the whole stream. Useful for a smoke test.
.TP
.BI \-\-attempts " N"
Attempts per chunk before giving up. Default:
.BR 6 .
Rate-limit and connection failures back off progressively, up to ten minutes
per wait; a deterministic failure such as a malformed URL aborts immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-split
Use a single edge node and a single worker.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-chunks
Keep the per-chunk
.I .ts
files after the concatenation succeeds.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mux
Download only. Leave the per-chunk
.I .ts
files in the work directory and skip the
.BR ffmpeg (1)
concat and remux.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print the resolved stream URL and the page title.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS The 2 MB/s ceiling, and why a browser is unaffected
Sustained download throughput from these edge nodes is capped at roughly
2.0 MB/s per client IP, and the cap is flat: one, two and four concurrent
fragments all measured 2.05 MB/s.
Short bursts are much faster than that, which is why a single segment can
appear to arrive at 5 MB/s while a long run settles at 2.
.P
The same CDN drops
.I new
TCP connection attempts for tens of seconds once too many are opened in a
short window; the client sees this as
.IR "No route to host" .
Connections that are already established are not affected.
This is why the web player keeps working while a downloader stalls: playback
needs about 1 MB/s against a 2 MB/s cap, and the player holds one long-lived
connection instead of opening a fresh one per segment.
A request that is already streaming is safe; a request that has to connect
during the window is not.

.SS The User-Agent requirement
The CDN answers 404 to any User-Agent that is not a current Linux Chrome
string, including
.BR yt\-dlp 's
own default.
.B cumcams-dl
therefore sends that string on every request it makes and passes it to
.BR yt\-dlp
with
.BR \-\-user\-agent .
This is why a hand-written
.B yt\-dlp
command against the same URL fails.
.SS Edge node discovery
The API returns one edge host such as
.I vi5b.cdnhlscloud.com
on
.IR 92.246.93.20 .
When
.B \-\-nodes
is greater than one,
.B cumcams-dl
probes the sibling letters under the same prefix and keeps the ones that
answer 200, so
.I vi5a
on
.IR 92.246.93.19
is added when reachable.
.SS Resume
Chunks are named
.IR NAME .0000.ts ,
.IR NAME .0001.ts ,
and so on.
A chunk whose file already exists and is larger than 1 KiB is skipped, so
re-running the same command continues where the previous run stopped.
Work directories live under
.I ${TMPDIR}/cumcams-dl-\fIID\fR
and are removed once the remux succeeds unless
.B \-\-keep\-chunks
or
.B \-\-no\-mux
is given.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.BR yt\-dlp
for the segment fetching.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR ffmpeg
unless
.B \-\-no\-mux
is used.
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3.10 or newer with the
.I requests
module.
.SH EXAMPLES
Download a show with the defaults:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play
.EE
.P
Send it somewhere else under a chosen name:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl \-o ~/Videos/cams \-n nana-2026-09-29 \e
    https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play
.EE
.P
Pull the first twenty minutes only, to check that the chain works:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl \-\-max\-segments 600 \-\-chunk\-size 300 \e
    https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play
.EE
.P
Recover from a CDN rate-limit: wait a few minutes, then re-run the identical
command. Completed chunks are skipped.
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play
.EE
.P
Keep the raw chunks instead of remuxing, to inspect or re-cut them:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl \-\-no\-mux \-\-keep\-chunks \e
    https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success: the remux was written, or
.B \-\-no\-mux
left the chunks in place.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: bad arguments, a dependency is missing, the page or API layout
changed, the playlist is encrypted, or a chunk exhausted its attempts.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with SIGINT. Re-running the same command resumes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Videos/cumcams
Default output directory.
.TP
.I ${TMPDIR}/cumcams-dl-\fIID\fR
Work directory holding chunk playlists and intermediate
.I .ts
files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH BUGS
The per-IP 2 MB/s ceiling cannot be raised by any client setting; more
concurrency does not help and can trip the connection shield.
A fully uninterrupted run is therefore not achievable at present: expect
interruptions, and let re-runs resume the remaining chunks.
Chunk-level resume is coarse: a chunk interrupted halfway is re-fetched from
its first segment.
Widevine or SAMPLE-AES protected playlists are refused rather than handled.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
